\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Parameter efficiency of LoRA fine-tuning across the three evaluated model architectures, demonstrating over 98\% reduction in trainable parameters. Furthermore, we extend our methodology by introducing \textbf  {Weight-Decomposed Low-Rank Adaptation (DoRA)} \cite  {liu2024dora}, which decomposes the pre-trained weights into magnitude and directional components for fine-tuning. This approach maintains the parameter efficiency of LoRA while achieving learning capacity closer to full fine-tuning. A visual comparison distinguishing LoRA's structure from DoRA's decomposed optimization is provided in Figure~\ref {fig:lora_efficiency}.}}{18}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:lora_efficiency}{{6}{18}{Parameter efficiency of LoRA fine-tuning across the three evaluated model architectures, demonstrating over 98\% reduction in trainable parameters. Furthermore, we extend our methodology by introducing \textbf {Weight-Decomposed Low-Rank Adaptation (DoRA)} \cite {liu2024dora}, which decomposes the pre-trained weights into magnitude and directional components for fine-tuning. This approach maintains the parameter efficiency of LoRA while achieving learning capacity closer to full fine-tuning. A visual comparison distinguishing LoRA's structure from DoRA's decomposed optimization is provided in Figure~\ref {fig:lora_efficiency}}{figure.caption.10}{}}
